{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Write.</b> But not orally, lest it come to forgetting over a long time, for its fulfillment depends on when a king of Israel shall reign, as it is written: והיה בהניח לך etc." "<b>This is a memorial in the book.</b> What Amalek did. For I want his infamy to be revealed, so that they will know why I blot him out. A memorial in the book — in the well-known book, and that is the Book of the Wars of YHWH. And in our sins it is not with us, just as we do not have the Book of Jashar. And the midrash of Eduth. And the words of the chronicles of the kings of Israel and the books of Solomon." "<b>And place in the ears of Yehoshua.</b> For he began the commandment, and he is to hand over this book of remembrance to the judge who comes after him as a memorial, and likewise judge after judge shall hand over this book of remembrance, until a king arises for Israel, and it shall be for a memorial, and they shall not wonder why I blot him out. And one should not interpret 'and place <b>in the ears of Yehoshua</b>' to mean to wage war against Amalek, for Israel did not fight him until Shaul." "<b>The remembrance of Amalek.</b> Because the chieftains of Edom, the leaders of Moav, Canaan, and Philistia panicked at the redemption from Egypt — but this one heard everything and came from a distant place to fight against them, and did not fear HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "\"ומדרש עדו\" is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. Possibly refers to a midrash on the word עדו or to a text called עדות."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:25.637374252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}